ronavirus no for this  particular condition that we're  discussing  the hepatitis c yes  um  i don't think there is a vaccine for  i i could be wrong but um i think the  main  result of the discovery of  hepatitis c was that it was possible to  check all blood  or contamination with this virus before  it was transfused  um and as far as treatment of people  who've actually  got hepatitis c i think  the the drugs that are now used very  successfully to cure  such individuals resulted from the work  done by charles rice  at the rockefeller where he successfully  cloned um the virus  and was able to undertake studies  in vitro with cultured human cells  liver cells and thereby  help the drug industry to develop  these combinations of drugs which are  curious  okay we'll leave it there dr gilbert  thompson talking to us on skype from  london good to talk to you sir thank you  very much  thank you
 

